itional independent polling or a surge of national Democratic spending could reveal a closer race; confirmation of Bice's lead in later surveys would push this toward Safe Republican.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Oklahoma's 5th District remains Republican territory, and incumbent Stephanie Bice enters the general election with the advantages that usually decide races here. The district leans Republican by about nine points, Bice has out-raised Democrat Jena Nelson roughly three to one, and every major race rating places the seat in the Safe or Likely Republican column. A Democratic-sponsored September poll showed Bice ahead by five points, closer than the district's lean but still behind.\n\nNelson, who won a contested primary, has drawn some national Democratic interest and the seat has been added to the party's target list, while prediction markets give her roughly a one-in-six chance. Bice has declined debate invitations, and two independents are also on the ballot. The evidence points to a Republican hold, with the main uncertainty being whether Democratic investment and a favorable midterm environment can narrow a structurally red district.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2